## Reviewer points not followed as worded

- ca-a #22 is right that Q16–Q20 read like a blog next to the Q1–Q15 headings. Not applied as new headings: the English source has the same bold lines and the same U+200B count, and the checker compares headings, blocks and ZWSP.
- ca-a #41 is right that "TWD 1.57M" is English abbreviation and that a Catalan dot is a thousands separator. Not applied: R12 and the pinned bio term forbid reformatting that figure.
- ca-a #27 is right that "per cada 1 any" is clumsy. In 008 the bare digit has to stay or the numbers check fails (missing 1×4). Wording around it is "1 any complet". "menys d’un any" did pass in 001 and 014.
- "per si mateix" is not always a gender error. It stays where the subject is masculine ("aquest article", "aquest escrit", "el fet"). "per si mateixa" / "per si mateixes" were already feminine and were left.
- "junts" is not always the English "together" calque. "treballen junts", "comparèixer junts" and "viure juntes" are ordinary Catalan and were left.
